{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And they shall take a bull, a son of the herd.</b> And it is a burnt-offering, as it is written ״and you shall make… and the one a burnt-offering״ — and it is a public offering for idolatry." "<b>And a second bull.</b> Why does Scripture say 'second'? To tell you: just as a burnt-offering is not eaten, so too a sin-offering is not eaten. And herein is support for his words in Sifrei; and I say that it was a provisional ruling — for they were supposed to bring a goat for a sin-offering for idolatry along with the bull of the burnt-offering."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {1 "Rashi preserves both a midrashic reading of 'second' and his own peshat alternative (a provisional ruling for that hour)."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:57.796978214Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}